>> title: Yellow Rice
>> category: Rice, Beans & Grains
>> tags: rice, turmeric, middle eastern, stock, side
>> counters: Shawarma Counter
>> aka: yellow rice, turmeric rice, seasoned rice, halal cart rice, cart rice, basmati rice, arroz amarillo, riz asfar
>> pairs-with: chicken-shawarma, white-sauce, rice-pilaf
>> servings: 6
>> time: 45 min
>> step.1: rinse until the water runs clear
>> step.2: bloom the turmeric and cumin in butter
>> step.3: toast the rice 2 min
>> step.4: simmer 15 min, lid on
>> step.5: steam off the heat 10 min, then fork

Rinse @basmati rice{2%cups}(400 g) in a bowl of cold water, pouring off and refilling four or five times until the water stops going white, then drain it well.

Bloom @ground turmeric{1 1/2%tsp}, @cumin seed{1%tsp} and @yellow onion{1%small}(diced fine) in @unsalted butter{3%Tbs}(45 g) in a #saucepan{} over medium heat ~fry{3%min}, until the butter is orange and the onion is soft.

Toast @&(~2)rinsed rice{} in @&(~1)spiced butter{} ~toast{2%min}, stirring, until every grain is coated and slightly translucent at the edge.

Simmer @chicken stock{3%cups}(700 mL) and @kosher salt{1 1/2%tsp} with @&(~1)toasted rice{}, covered, over the lowest heat ~simmer{15%min}.

Take @&(~1)rice{} off the heat and let it ~steam{10%min} with the lid still on and undisturbed, then fork it through.
